      <FormatDescription>In the original 2007 specification, internal files had the structure:

fe_2007_&lt;extent&gt;_&lt;layer&gt;.&lt;extension&gt;

However, from 2008 the naming convention changed to:

tl_YYYY_&lt;extent&gt;_&lt;layer&gt;.&lt;extension&gt;

Further, TIGER/Line files related to Congressional Districts and Redistricting Data may follow the naming convention:

tl_rdYY_&lt;extent&gt;_&lt;layer&gt;.&lt;extension&gt;

‘YYYY’ or ‘YY’ represents the year the data was produced. ‘Extent’ is a 2-5 digit value representing a geographical area. ‘Layer’ specifies the type of geography or feature that the file contains. ‘Extension’ refers to the specific file type, usually .shp, .dbf, .cpg, .shx, or .prj.</FormatDescription>
